{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science","id":1290315,"title":"How does consensual reality work if people disbelieve even science?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-21T06:12:33-08:00","id":1290315,"title":"How does consensual reality work if people disbelieve even science?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> I am a player of Mage the Awakening and just found out Ascension, and I got confused about the Consensual Reality and how it works, I will copy (and edit) texts from other people which exposes my doubts really well:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">People in the world are religious and therefore, you should be able to use magic without a problem if you disguise it as miracles. <i>Tons</i> of people believe in ghosts, psychics, paranormal phenomena or outright believe in magic and witchcraft. Distrust in science is so high that a large part of people <i>disbelieve in evolution, vaccines, and the moon landing.</i><br /> <br /> In other words, consensus simply does not work as presented in Mage books. It's a broken idea. People simply aren't that logical and rational. We're a superstitious, religious lot that believes in magic, miracles and the paranormal.<br /> <br /> If people don't really believe in science, then there should be nothing &quot;backing&quot; the scientific consensus. Because this is all about belief. Either people do believe (in which case you've got a majority of religious people - shouldn't be too hard to convince them that there's a new breed of holy men), they don't believe (but then the scientific paradigm is not backed up by anything anyway, so why should it inflict Paradox?) or people do believe in the scientific paradigm as a majority (and that is not the state of the world).<br /> <br /> The thing about evolution is about just how much people distrust science. This isn't about laws of reality. Remember, <i>there aren't any laws of reality</i> - there's just the Consensus. And here's the deal: people just aren't that enthusiastic about it. And this means that there's just not that much belief behind it. People need to believe, <i>truly believe</i>, to make a paradigm the dominant one. Science just isn't backed by this sort of belief and public trust. Whereas, there's tons of belief behind religions, which means that if you adjust your magic to fit the religious paradigm or claim to be psychic, the majority of people should buy that explanation.</div>Unless I am missing something, nothing should work in the Mage cosmology, if this has been answered somewhere please point me in that direction.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the time and attention,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-21-2019, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T07:35:33-08:00","id":1290341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ibeaumanior</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If people don't really believe in anything, then there should be nothing &quot;backing&quot; the <b>scientific consensus</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not a scientific consensus, there's a <i>Technocratic</i> consensus. It may <i>sound </i>similar, but it's very different and, I think, it's the key of making sense to Mage.<br /> <br /> Mage doesn't have to make sense, but it <i>can </i>make sense. I'm not postulating that Mage, as the Authors tought about it, makes sense. This vision isn't necessarily the same that the Authors have and it's not canon (but it's 100% compatible with the canon, as far as I know), it's just how I see this stuff.<br /> <br /> Having said that:<br /> <br /> &quot;Belief&quot; it's not just how you <i>explain </i>the world, it's something deeper that has to do with how you &quot;act&quot; upon the world (this is very well represented in M20 by the tripartite division between Paradigm, <i>Practice </i>and <i>Tools</i>). At a deeper level all humans make jumps of faith. It's usefull to think about this in David Hume's terms: People doesn't have any proof that the sun will raise tomorrow - most people just can't grasp the physics needed to demonstrate this even if we accepted causality (which Hume doesn't) - yet people believe that the sun raises every day just because it always has done so. This is not a <i>logical reason</i>, but a falacy. Hence people believe in this w/o proof aka Faith. People always pay lip service to a lot of beliefs, but those beliefs they <i>act </i>upon, I think, run deeper.<br /> <br /> So, I would say that the Technocratic Consensus it's there because people, in the deepest sense that there is,<i> believe in technology</i>:<br /> <br /> Devout Christians, Buddhists and Umbanda practicioners alike would use a car to travel than ask for milacurous teleportation (even when the latter would be much more practical !). A devout christian may not understand or believe in the internal working of the machine, but they do believe cars are the most convinient way to travel and asking an angel to take them to the church would be totaly out of the question unless there's the dirests of needs (and even then probably they will pray for a taxi rather than teleportation - and that's probably Coincident <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> This may be not becuase they believe milacres don't exist but because they believe they're rare, difficult, that God's name shouldn't be invoked in vain, or that they're not holly enough to deserve it...so be it, the Traditions dug their own graves when they decided to make their milacres &quot;special&quot;.<br /> <br /> Our practicioners of Santeria believe in guns so much that they have a saint that you can pray to protect you against bullets...and, really, that's nonsense if guns weren't effective and fearsome to begin with.<br /> <br /> All you need to have the Consensus up and running it's the majority of the populace of a given area to believe that your mojo <i>works. The Consensus doesn't</i> <i>care about the why and hows </i>as long as the people of the Reality Zone can rationalize it <i>somehow</i>.<br /> Obviously, the Technocracy does care about the why and how becuase they doesn't want merely to be accepted by the Consensus but also to exlude everyone else's - and <b>this </b>they haven't achieved, as M20 clearly states - but as long as there's more people fighting with guns than people fighting with inchantations, technology remains on top (even if they believe that guns work trough incantation).<br /> <br /> The Technocracy burried the idea that guns, planes, and cars function by using them when they were still Vulgar. They accepted (not always voluntarily, though) to blow themselves and their minions up in the face of unbelievers until &quot;guns are effective&quot; was hammered in the minds of enough people as to constitute a bulkward against Paradox.<br /> <br /> People believe in (most of) technology because technology just works. In our world this is because what science says holds water (most of the time). In Mage this is because the Technocracy and normal humans pushed it 'til it worked. And even then, failures and nasty consequences of technology are sometimes atributed to a form of Paradox in the canon - and in M20 the concept of Reality Zone allows to create places where technology it's unreliable (often these are remote enough that failure can be atributed to technological necesities like &quot;having signal&quot;).<br /> <br /> The examples you mention can be explained: I doubt most people disbelieve in the moon landing, but even if they did most people aren't in the position of traveling there (and those who are work in an environment where nobody doubts it). Evolution it's simply a theory, a theory can never be Vulgar - the Consensus enters in scene when you <i>do </i>stuff. If the anty-vaxers won the populace, in Mage vaccines would start having problems and eventually cease to function, but since medicine it's still a major part of life in advanced cities (even if most people would thank God, they usually do what the medic says), I would wage that these places aren't that well connected, don't have a lot of people (Consensus counts people, not area) and thus can be either superseeded by the global Consensus or made into Reality Zones (the Technocracy's job hasn't ended there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-21-2019, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:22:41-08:00","id":1290386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science#post1290315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> I am a player of Mage the Awakening and just found out Ascension, and I got confused about the Consensual Reality and how it works, I will copy (and edit) texts from other people which exposes my doubts really well:[INDENT]People in the world are religious and therefore, you should be able to use magic without a problem if you disguise it as miracles. <i>Tons</i> of people believe in ghosts, psychics, paranormal phenomena or outright believe in magic and witchcraft. Distrust in science is so high that a large part of people <i>disbelieve in evolution, vaccines, and the moon landing.</i><br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Thanks for the time and attention,</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a subject that is brought up periodically, because you are correct the consensus can't be as simple as it first seems. There is more that has to be going on that people often do not realize, and some things that can't be going on that people often assume. Some that come to mind:<br /> <br /> - Aleph has already covered one of the biggest, that 'belief' is about a lot more than religious like levels of belief. Even people who think the world is flat expect the lights to come on when they hit a switch. <br /> - The same person can believe two contradictory things without realizing it.<br /> - People are extremely good at rationalizing away brief impossibilities. How many times have you seen something impossible only to realize it was a trick of the light? It happens to me quite a bit, especially when I am driving in the dark. There can be strange happenings without the world looking completely different.<br /> - The consensus is not as simple as &quot;if more people believe X than Y, X is true and Y is not. <br /> - The same event can actually back up two completely contradictory beliefs.<br /> - Beliefs and expectations don't change over night.<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can dig up some of the threads where we've examined this before. I don't promise they will answer your questions, but you can at least see how we've approached this issue before. <br /> <br /> In the meantime, though, let me turn the question around on you. You use evolution, vaccines, and the moon landing as your examples of things the consensus is undermining. If you are right and support for them is wavering or collapsing, what would you expect to see happen in the WoD?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:54:39-08:00","id":1290406,"title":"","content":"Thanks both for the answers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1290386#post1290386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll see if I can dig up some of the threads where we've examined this before. I don't promise they will answer your questions, but you can at least see how we've approached this issue before.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, though, let me turn the question around on you. You use evolution, vaccines, and the moon landing as your examples of things the consensus is undermining. If you are right and support for them is wavering or collapsing, what would you expect to see happen in the WoD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would expect more return to a pastoral idealization, where everything organic and natural is benign. A romanticized view of the world. I am not saying the Technocracy is right however, just that there is a gap, if you will, between what we would consider magical thinking and rational thinking, that has not been filled even in industrialized countries. By that criteria, the United States (a very industrialized country by any metric) is also one of the most superstitious one (beliefs in UFOs, angels, psychics, mediums, crystal healing, etc)<br /> <br /> My question is how did the actual consensus ever got to be THE Consensus, given that people have always been superstitious, most of them wouldn't understand high school science, and even as I write this, large swaths of the population are actively anti-science (with my examples of moon landing, evolution, faith healers, and many others)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:05:12-08:00","id":1290434,"title":"","content":"We should also circle around the assumption that dissent from actual scientific fact is representative of a disbelief in science. Modernist argumentation values scientific evidence, rationality, etc. - this is the cornerstone of the Technocratic paradigm. But if it turns out we were 100% dead wrong about, say, photons, that would not render prior statements about them &quot;unscientific&quot; - a paradigm has to do with what we consider valuable argumentation, interpretation, and evidence, and not the factual outcome of investigation.<br /> <br /> Remember that Intelligent Design proponents make assertions from geology, the fossil record, ergonomics (see the infamous 'banana' example) - we may believe that they are inwardly insincere, but their disagreement agrees with the (paradigmatic) rules of engagement. They're wrong about the facts, sure, but they are approaching their assertions by positing &quot;scientific&quot; facts to contradict the evolutionary model, and argue that the theory of evolution is not in accord with reason. They agree with the underlying paradigm of argumentation, but dispute the facts. Many of them think that <i>we </i>are the ones being irrational and unscientific, in fact.<br /> <br /> Most of the people who buy magnetic bracelets wouldn't buy them if you said they were magic. They've been bamboozled by an argument in a paradigm they find convincing - the assertion of &quot;rational scientific principles&quot; which do not accord with the facts, but do accord with the paradigm of valid assertions.<br /> <br /> Paradigms are models of interpretation, not bundles of facts - you can be a proponent of Intelligent Design or a faked moon landing or vaccines causing autism or UFOs and still be in accord with the Technocratic paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:27:51-08:00","id":1290446,"title":"","content":"G<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1290406#post1290406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks both for the answers.<br /> <br /> My question is how did the actual consensus ever got to be THE Consensus, given that people have always been superstitious, most of them wouldn't understand high school science, and even as I write this, large swaths of the population are actively anti-science (with my examples of moon landing, evolution, faith healers, and many others)</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, here are two of the threads I mentioned earlier. The first is a question of how a specific concept entered the Consensus, the other is a search for a way the consensus could work and still give us a world like we see in Mage.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus\">Doctor Johnathan Snow and that Pesky Consensus</a> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality\">Working From First Principles: Subjective Reality</a><br /> <br /> Getting back to your points, when I think of something like vaccines breaking down I think the first signs would be something more like what we saw two years ago, when the flu vaccines had an abyssmal success rate because they predicted the wrong strain for that year. Obviously lack of belief has nothing to do with that in the real world, but the two pair together quite well in Mage if that's the way you want to go. Strangely enough, belief in evolution or the moon landing don't affect things much in Mage. Evolution because it normally operates on a longer time scale than the vast majority of games, and the moon landing because it happened in the past. If the disbelief were more focused on genetics or rocketry that would likely have a bigger impact.<br /> <br /> As for how the current consensus became the consensus, I attribute it to several things. First, it takes a lot of 'belief' to make something an everyday part of life, but not that much to make it happen occasionally. That sets up a situation where evidence for something can start forming before it is widely believed. Second, as others have said, people only have to believe that something works and that there is some kind of reason for it, they don't have to know or understand the reason. Third, people actually want to have explanations for the world (even if they don't want to have to learn the details) and to believe they have an element of control. In regards to that the modern paradigm offers the most bang for the least buck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:42:09-08:00","id":1290454,"title":"","content":"I remember reading a quote on this forum...<br /> <br /> &quot;There are buddhists who believe that through perfect harmony with the world they could teleport, pause time, levitate or all sorts of wonderful things. These people use cars, planes and modern medicine.&quot;<br /> <br /> Practically EVERYONE outside of tiny uncontacted communities in the Amazon and similar believes in a sort of &quot;scientific consensus&quot;, even if it's one they don't claim to understand. For many it goes as far as &quot;cars/computers/planes work because I know they work&quot;. However these people have additional beliefs layered on top of scientific belief. They believe in cars, but they also believe in the &quot;old roads&quot; that connect spiritual places. That sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T15:17:43-08:00","id":1290552,"title":"","content":"That's the reason the Technocracy has to murder all the magicians. Its the only way people accept science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:51:37-08:00","id":1290594,"title":"","content":"I think the best way to use it in my game is consensual reality isn't a thing for non-mages.<br /> <br /> Reality isn't made by Sleepers.<br /> <br /> Sleepers, however, make sure that you can't affect reality in front of them.<br /> <br /> Their collective 7,000,000 Muggle brains make sure that 1 guys' attempts to throw lightning doesn't work.<br /> <br /> But their collective doesn't make the rest of reality.<br /> <br /> It just keeps you from affecting it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1290552#post1290552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the reason the Technocracy has to murder all the magicians. Its the only way people accept science.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're handling it in a backass way because, of course, making people believe what is not true is the definition of not science. They also repeatedly back pseudo-science from Star Trek and get mad people don't believe it in any more than faith healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T00:44:14-08:00","id":1290679,"title":"","content":"My own musings on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus\">the nature of the Consensus</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T02:07:31-08:00","id":1290699,"title":"","content":"I have read more about the topic, and it seems this is a frequent topic among the fanbase, I would have hoped that by M20 the developers would have done something to handle it, like:&quot;there is a basic reality and the consensus influences it&quot;<br /> <br /> Because, as it stands, it seems the Technocracy is right... Worse than that, it seems that Mage is internally inconsistent, unlike say Vampire or Werewolf.<br /> <br /> How did hunter gatherers EVER get to the scientific method if the Consensus shapes reality? Unless there IS some default state (scientific paradigm?) and from there you deviate (jesus, even the description sounds Technocratic) using the Consensual Reality effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-22-2019, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T03:35:47-08:00","id":1290708,"title":"","content":"Reality is not 100% the Consensus and vice versa. There are baselines, this is how Sorcerers, Vampires, Werewolves etc can exist without Paradox. This is what they call &quot;Static&quot; magic, sometimes its more powerful than what a mage may be able to produce at a given time, sometimes it's not. These form the rules that are built into Reality of which science/technology (small s) is one small collective method of those rules as it passes from a Dynamic state into a Stasis state (eventually all things fall to Entropy), or if you prefer this is part of the Weaver's direct influence on the world via humanity. <br /> <br /> These small collectives of rules that allow for static magic are where we get the beginnings of a Mage. This is where the pre-initiates of the Order of Hermes come from, the non-awakened Druids and so forth. The Awakening isn't of course necessarily linked to these things or people doing these things but what it does do is provide the Mage with a sudden understanding of Reality or The Tapestry and that some of these collective rules can actually be used beyond their limited scope to literally re-write the Tapestry to the mage's desires. True Magick / Awakened Magick. Now the Tapestry can endure minor tweaks but doesn't like being unraveled and rewoven and this provides Scourge which would later become / be replaced by Paradox. Now this is where the Consensus comes in. The little rules collectively called sciences are a part of Reality as we know, and some Mages Awakened not to spells and spirits and so on, but to the functional Possibilities of what the rules of science could achieve. This becomes Enlightened Science as inspired by Genius and the Order of Reason worked on the public perception enough that they provided access to science to the masses at the exclusion of the other small rules. The Consensus was always present in some way, shape or form with what the masses in an area functionally believed. However the Order of Reason got people with a focused true belief on an as yet unseen scale and (given that every human alive is a potential mage, plus the way the umbrae work) this changed what were locally effective consensuses into the Consensus, built off of what everyone experiences every day on a fundamental level and then taking it up from there. With this achieved (and while ti was being worked on) they could then start thrusting a wedge into the Tapestry and its rules so that acts of Enlightened Science would gradually become part of the Static Rules while everything else becomes rarely seen and forgotten / disbelieved in. <br /> <br /> What you end up with after all this is a Tapestry of Reality that has been slowly rewoven into something entirely different. One that is readily accepting of minor tweaks only now those tweaks take a certain theme and form consistently &amp; globally more often (but not exclusively) than regionally or locally. However despite this the Static Rules / magic exploited by supernatural creatures and sorcerers and the existence of the umbrae and so on are still there and the rules and methods of magick are also still there. This is where the tagline of &quot;Reality is a Lie&quot; comes from and is the very core nature of the Ascension War because the Consensus is an artificial construct that spans the physical world created, maintained and enforced by the Technocratic Union which provides a world they can more readily control [We. Are. Control] and a battleground against those they cannot control &lt;Control is a Technocratic illusion, data is supposed to be free 00100010111011000222&gt; of their own choosing. The truth is that the Consensus is massively ingrained in people and the Tapestry now with things they simply do not want to let go of making it rather powerful. But it's also fragile and not because science (or even Science) is going to stop working, but because magick even after 2+ centuries of Consensus hasn't gone away. It is possible that it can work its way back in and not necessarily by replacing science in the rules but by providing options beyond what science can do and outside of the Technocratic Paradigm. It creates people who challenge and question and seek challenges and questions and maybe in that sparks more Avatars into Awakening or simply shifts the Consensus just a little bit and some of that Enlightened Science becomes a little less reliable because it's no longer a tweak in a carefully constructed Tapestry but a re-weave of a less predictable one. Again here is the nature of the Ascension War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:32:44-08:00","id":1290734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1290699#post1290699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have read more about the topic, and it seems this is a frequent topic among the fanbase, I would have hoped that by M20 the developers would have done something to handle it, like:&quot;there is a basic reality and the consensus influences it&quot;<br /> <br /> Because, as it stands, it seems the Technocracy is right... Worse than that, it seems that Mage is internally inconsistent, unlike say Vampire or Werewolf.<br /> <br /> How did hunter gatherers EVER get to the scientific method if the Consensus shapes reality? Unless there IS some default state (scientific paradigm?) and from there you deviate (jesus, even the description sounds Technocratic) using the Consensual Reality effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea it's that STs decides what's true and what isn't. This can be seen in how Earthly Foundations are handled in M20, and also with the writeup of Universal Constants in Revised: Foundations work because people it's accustomed to them or because they ARE a part of reality that sits above and beyond the Consensus? - the book implies that botha re possible.<br /> <br /> Personally, I follow a cosmology where, much like <i>Moirdryd </i>puts it, the Consensus doesn't control all of the universe. You can see my opinion in one of the threads that were mentioned. The Consensus, Humanity, it's a powerful force that warps and shapes the world, but it didn't created the baseline Reality. In my view the Pures, shards of the One, created the baseline rules, which sometimes agrees with science(Gravity, Electromagnetism) and sometimes doesn't (spirits, Quintessence).<br /> <br /> However, there's proof going either way, so ultimately there's no such thing as the &quot;truth of Mage&quot;. You're free to choose between the premises. After all, inconsistency it's, logically speaking, an allowance to chose any premise (when &quot;it's falsum&quot; no premise can be said to be true or false by logic alone, hence nothing changes if you choose one or another).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-22-2019, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:46:11-08:00","id":1290740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1290699#post1290699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have read more about the topic, and it seems this is a frequent topic among the fanbase, I would have hoped that by M20 the developers would have done something to handle it, like:&quot;there is a basic reality and the consensus influences it&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a solution, though. I would fight like hell to keep that from ever being the solution. Which is not to say that it's not a valid way of playing the game, but it is needlessly limiting to make it the only way of playing Mage. It takes away one of the elements that a lot of fans find extremely enjoyable and unique about Mage. There's no benefit to making that kind of change .<br /> <br /> Plus we'd also lose out on these great forum conversations. They may not be one of the intended purposes of the game but they are no bad thing as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because, as it stands, it seems the Technocracy is right... Worse than that, it seems that Mage is internally inconsistent, unlike say Vampire or Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>The tagline of Mage is an Epic Game of Reality on the Brink. While we may dislike the idea of internal inconsistency, it actually benefits the mood and themes of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How did hunter gatherers EVER get to the scientific method if the Consensus shapes reality? Unless there IS some default state (scientific paradigm?) and from there you deviate (jesus, even the description sounds Technocratic) using the Consensual Reality effects. </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting phenomenon. Almost every time I see someone postulate some kind of default state of reality their very next idea is that it would be the scientific or modern paradigm. It makes sense that that would be the first to come to mind since that is what we are familiar with, but it's not the best choice for a baseline. It's too defined for one, which means it forces more changes on the game. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T07:48:00-08:00","id":1290757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1290740#post1290740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus we'd also lose out on these great forum conversations. They may not be one of the intended purposes of the game but they are no bad thing as far as I'm concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, they're not.<br /> <br /> Here I will leave a thread with mad theories about the cosmology of mage. It includes a particularly mad theory of my own (that's by no means how I think things &quot;actually&quot; work, btw). I think the thread it's relevant to &quot;alternate&quot; understandings of Mage and has very good debates about consensual reality and it's reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon\"> Could I get some people to poke holes in my Head-Canon? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> SO, I'll admit I'm a bit of a latecomer to mage. And while I've somewhat voraciously torn into the setting there are some books I don't have, and some knowledge about the setting I simply lack. For example? Voormas's Exploits. I know some of what happened but fairly little. Anyway, My Head-Canon largely relies on a couple simple things. 1.) The Anthropic Principle/Subjective Reality. For this Head-Canon to work, Reality must fundamentally be determined by what people believe. There cannot be any deeper secret of 'how reality works' than 'this is what people believe and so it's true.' This one is </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-22-2019, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T16:04:31-08:00","id":1290927,"title":"","content":"I found this text in the <b>Book of Secrets</b>:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Victory, for the Technocratic Union, has nothing to do<br /> with the number of people who use computers. It\u2019s based on<br /> the extermination of Reality Deviants and the pacification<br /> of the Masses. <b>If the Technocracy had won, there\u2019d be no<br /> vampires, no werewolves, no Banes or rival mages, no Daesh,<br /> Internet trolling, </b>or popular media based on wizards<b>. A victorious<br /> Technocracy would grind religious fundamentalism<br /> down while making clean air and water available for everyone.<br /> Science classes would be mandatory, and politicians<br /> who slash school funding would be retired, reformed, or<br /> replaced. HIT Marks would be mowing down Daesh</b>, not<br /> obscure Goddess cultists.</i></div>The more I read about it, the less I see problems with the Technocracy (except for a limited art expression). Seriously, I was into the traditions, and it seems that the Technocracy are the good guys? Confused emoji","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-22-2019, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T18:51:08-08:00","id":1290956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1290927#post1290927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The more I read about it, the less I see problems with the Technocracy (except for a limited art expression). Seriously, I was into the traditions, and it seems that the Technocracy are the good guys? Confused emoji</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because the Technocracy's solution to Internet Trolling is to Send in Hitmarks and/or drag the person off to Room 101. IT has MANY good features its all a matter of what its doing in the name of those things and whether the price they claim is necissary. Nothing.. does stop them from sending their Hitmarks to Murder Every Vampire in their sleep... yet they focus on mages first. Even a mage sitting in the middle of nowhere just practicing magic in the woods..that person can't be left alone even though there' are thousands of vampires hurting the masses..<br /> <br /> Nothing about providing a good living, clean air/water forces them to hunt down fellow mages. One might even say if they spent all the resources on the Pogrom providing a better future they be closer there.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is of course.. before we hit the horror show that is the Syndicate who says &quot;We need to make a profit on this&quot; and who are totally providing CLean air and water..at a price.. they will totally sell you back what should have been FREE after they've made money poluting the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T19:28:56-08:00","id":1290969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1290927#post1290927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found this text in the <b>Book of Secrets</b>:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Victory, for the Technocratic Union, has nothing to do<br /> with the number of people who use computers. It\u2019s based on<br /> the extermination of Reality Deviants and the pacification<br /> of the Masses. <b>If the Technocracy had won, there\u2019d be no<br /> vampires, no werewolves, no Banes or rival mages, no Daesh,<br /> Internet trolling, </b>or popular media based on wizards<b>. A victorious<br /> Technocracy would grind religious fundamentalism<br /> down while making clean air and water available for everyone.<br /> Science classes would be mandatory, and politicians<br /> who slash school funding would be retired, reformed, or<br /> replaced. HIT Marks would be mowing down Daesh</b>, not<br /> obscure Goddess cultists.</i></div>The more I read about it, the less I see problems with the Technocracy (except for a limited art expression). Seriously, I was into the traditions, and it seems that the Technocracy are the good guys? Confused emoji</div> </div> </div> </div>Consensual Reality Doesn't Make Sense, Science is the Default Reality, <i>and</i> The Technocracy Are the Real Good Guys in a single thread? If you bring up HAP vs HOP I think I win Mage Forum Bingo. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all seriousness, there's a lot to like about the Technocracy. They have some very noble ideals and dream of a lot of good things for humanity. They are also the poster children for Noble Cause Corruption. They want good things but they do terrible things to get them. It's even creeping into the section you read, not just in the motivations but the terminology. It's the same way for the Traditions, they want freedom and choice and to raise up the potential of all people, but they are willing to keep the doors open for a lot of terrible things in the name of that enlightenment. It's not that either group is blind to their failings, it is that they think there will be time to fix them later. They may even be right.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T19:30:40-08:00","id":1290970,"title":"","content":"To be fair, The Technocracy Are the Real Good Guys is the Free Square of Mage Forum Bingo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:39:08-08:00","id":1291067,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy believe that they have the moral high ground. That their way - of One Reality - is unequivocally the correct one, and that everyone else are dangerous lunatics. The Technocratic Union believes they, alone, are right.<br /> <br /> That righteousness allows them to rationalize a bottomless well of sins. They believe they have the Answer, ergo any underhanded act done in service to that answer is worth the price.<br /> <br /> Not even getting into how their centuries of success have bred both complacency and corruption. The Syndicate, for instance, doesn't even really believe that Mass Ascension is actually possible. They are content to create a world that is merely comfortable and convenient for Sleepers, even as it sinks those same Sleepers into their stupors. If they can make money for themselves along the way, even better. Then you have the New World Order, which actively brainwashed Union members for years, just to prevent them from speaking, acting, or thinking contrary to the Union's official policy. If the ones at the top had their way, there would BE no free thought, for fear of even the possibility of treachery or deviance.<br /> <br /> Of course the Union isn't irredeemable. They have many good points (just ask a Progenitor about why stuff like faith healing or alternative medicine is dangerous). And, especially in the Revised era and beyond, you see many of the idealistic Technocrats, who operate on the front lines, forcing changes on the system that makes the Union less abominable. (Like, for instance, Iteration X getting more compact brain implants, so they can get some of their brain meats put back in, that controlled empathy and shit). But that was a change that was only necessary <i>because</i> the Union had become so corrupt, and drifted away from their high minded goals.<br /> <br /> Further, many of those systemic problems still remained, because the Union was founded on the idea that if they crush all mysticism and displace the superstitionists, that a perfect world will naturally fall into place. A belief that not only allows them to justify any sort of activity, but also blinds them to the problems inherent in the industrial society they spent so long building. Blind to the excesses of corporations, the abuses of government, and the new vistas of abuse and depravity that can arise from new technology like the Internet (and the failure of businesses and systems to tackle such problems on an individual level, because it would be &quot;too hard&quot; or cost too much money).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:49:14-08:00","id":1291069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1290969#post1290969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Consensual Reality Doesn't Make Sense, Science is the Default Reality, <i>and</i> The Technocracy Are the Real Good Guys in a single thread? If you bring up HAP vs HOP I think I win Mage Forum Bingo. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What is HOP / HAP?<br /> <br /> And I see the points related but I am not an expert in the lore, for me, as an Awakening player the point is/was: findout what is right and do that (the main problem in Awakening is nobody is sure what is right); here it <i>seems</i> that whatever the Technocracy aims end up being (as stated in that paragraph, by the developers) would be considered an improvement, and ties with my (admittedly skewed) idea of what is good for mankind in the WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T05:03:50-08:00","id":1291091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1291069#post1291069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is HOP / HAP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh. Okay, let's take it from the top.<br /> <br /> HOP: Hypothetical Omniscient Observer<br /> HAP: Hypothetical Average Observer<br /> <br /> These are two ways that the rules for Magick can be interpreted, when it comes to Effects being Coincidental or Vulgar. This deriving from the idea that we're judging it according to a hypothetical observer, against whom the mage is trying to fool.<br /> <br /> With HOP, you assume that the observer is functionally omniscient. They can see into your pockets, have night vision, perfectly understand physics and biology (and can see them in action), and otherwise has no limits to what it can know about what you, the mage, are up to. It's not a stretch to assume that under HOP, basically nothing is Coincidental, because the Hypothetical Observer has perfect knowledge of the situation and how the mage is violating the Consensus.<br /> <br /> With HAP, you assume an observer that is a normal, average human being, who believes all the most widely believed aspects of the Consensus. The cannot see in your pockets, they cannot see in the dark, they cannot tell water from vodka at a glance (though they may be able to smell the difference), and they don't see a bone-cracking punch as being anything more than a punch. Most people - including the designers behind M20 - seem to agree that this is preferable, as it gives a more interesting latitude for players and storytellers to operate. Because it's actually possible for an Effect to be Coincidental, so long as the mage is clever. It rewards lateral thinking, sleight of hand, and novel interpretations of both Spheres and Instruments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T05:56:25-08:00","id":1291104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science#post1290315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Tons</i> of people believe in ghosts, psychics, paranormal phenomena or outright believe in magic and witchcraft. Distrust in science is so high that a large part of people <i>disbelieve in evolution, vaccines, and the moon landing.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that why magick still works? Because Consensus isn't crystalized in reasonable facts. Yet.<br /> At least that's the way I made it work in my head.<br /> The Chorister can work miracles because somewhere someone believes that miracles exist.<br /> Same goes for the Science! of an Etherite. Somewhere someone believes that making a frankenstein monster is possible. That someone might even be just the Etherite himself, and if enough strong-willed it will work anyway<br /> <br /> Also it's, I think, one of the reasons they changed back the setting from revised-era banality (or was it apathy?): increase in real world &quot;believers&quot;<br /> which I think it would make an historical chronicle set in the '90s much cooler, calling it &quot;the Age of Banality&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T07:59:16-08:00","id":1291133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1291069#post1291069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is HOP / HAP?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1291091#post1291091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh. Okay, let's take it from the top.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I mean by Mage Forum Bingo. There are certain topics that have a tendency to run out of control. People who have seen them before tend to brace for impact when they see them, but they also draw people in because there are strong opinions about them. Even now, I have a strong urge to correct what Bluecho said about HOP, even though this isn't a HAP/HOP thread. These topics have a life of their own.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy Are the Real Good Guys is another one, because it often involves people skewing what one side or the other is about. Often it won't be too long before you get a small group of people insisting that the Traditions want to take humanity back to the dark ages or that the Technocracy wants to turn the world into an Orwellian nightmare. Neither of those is true. At worst the two are only wiling to risk those outcomes happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1291069#post1291069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I see the points related but I am not an expert in the lore, for me, as an Awakening player the point is/was: findout what is right and do that (the main problem in Awakening is nobody is sure what is right); here it <i>seems</i> that whatever the Technocracy aims end up being (as stated in that paragraph, by the developers) would be considered an improvement, and ties with my (admittedly skewed) idea of what is good for mankind in the WoD</div> </div> </div> </div>I am seeing some of your issue. While there are some broad similarities, Awakening and Ascension are very different games. The overall conflict of the Pentacle vs the Seers could be loosely described as 'is it better to try to escape the prison or butter up the jailers?' That's not what's going on between the Traditions and the Technocracy. That fight is an ideological one about Freedom vs Security.<br /> <br /> You mention that in Awakening no one knows what is right. That's true in Ascension as well. It's one of the themes even. You have phenomenal cosmic power but are no better situated to tell right from wrong than anyone else. What do you do? How much are you willing to fight for your ideals? What are you willing to sacrifice? As Exhibit A we have a faction that sees humanity as the most important thing in the world and wants to see them dominate the world and is willing to manipulate them, stomp out their dreams, indoctrinate them, and take away what makes them human to see it happen. As Exhibit B we have a faction that sees humanity as the most important thing in the world and wants to see them rise to the very heights of enlightenment and creativity, and is willing to let them fall, be preyed upon by monsters, and live in a chaotic world if that is the price. Both the Traditions and the Technocracy are high minded idealists with a heaping helping of moral flaws.<br /> <br /> People new to the game often initially see the Traditions as the clear good guys and the Technocracy as the clear bad guys and get surprised when they realize the Technocracy has a lot going for it. They've come a long way from the early days of Mage when they were just reality dominating villains. Just remember, they are also a bunch of well intentioned extremists who are willing to do terrible things if it comes to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-23-2019, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:29:48-08:00","id":1291177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1291133#post1291133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People new to the game often initially see the Traditions as the clear good guys and the Technocracy as the clear bad guys and get surprised when they realize the Technocracy has a lot going for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny. I usually have the opposite problem when I introduce people to the setting.<br /> They don't get why the Technocracy aren't the good guys.<br /> Maybe the newest gamers are a more pragmatic bunch and the Technocracy philosophy is more aligned with the way they think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:56:58-08:00","id":1291187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1291177#post1291177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny. I usually have the opposite problem when I introduce people to the setting.<br /> They don't get why the Technocracy aren't the good guys.<br /> Maybe the newest gamers are a more pragmatic bunch and the Technocracy philosophy is more aligned with the way they think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, despite the 90s being known as the time of disenchantment, gamers of the time were remarkably Romantic. At least compared to the completely cynical bastards of today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:05:05-08:00","id":1291192,"title":"","content":"I had that once Ravnos and so we approached that perspective philosophy. It was great, we started with a special session Zero and the players were excited to be doing this or that. Then we got to assigning their Conventions three got what they wanted, two got where their abilities were more useful. They didn't like that as much but rolled with it, did a couple of sessions then got given an assignment from above after a review, on this assignment three members of the group (one in their chosen convention two outside) were told outright they couldn't do anything above a 2 Sphere effect (in IC terms). Period. They didn't get to ask why and certainly got no explanations. They get through the assignment. They learn a bunch of stuff over the next couple of sessions and get told what they can and cannot act upon. This chafes a bit and they bend a few rules to do what they want. They get a formal warning (complete with MiB visitation from within the NWO) that if they keep acting like radicals they will be designated as such. As such they get given their schedules for the next week which limits their activities to those designated by Control and all the attached paperwork. <br /> <br /> The game ran for another few sessions, plenty of small plots got wrapped up, they had fun with it. But by the end of it they got WHY the Technocracy is considered a &quot;bad guy&quot; in the core game theme. They played regular mages in the next MTA game we did a few months later and said that they felt liberated compared to the Technocratic game. I did point out it's not always 100% like that but lots of the Union do tend to go that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:09:43-08:00","id":1291196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1291133#post1291133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People new to the game often initially see the Traditions as the clear good guys and the Technocracy as the clear bad guys and get surprised when they realize the Technocracy has a lot going for it. They've come a long way from the early days of Mage when they were just reality dominating villains. Just remember, they are also a bunch of well intentioned extremists who are willing to do terrible things if it comes to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of Phil Brucato's musings about the Fascist Urge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20: Book of Secrets - P. 290</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone who pursues and achieves significant influence over other people faces the potential corruption of power and authority. It's not hard to envision an occult struggle for earthly Reality as a clash of metaphysical fascist sects. Real-world occultism has a long history of groups whose totalitarian goals were cloaked in benevolent ideals, and the people who join such sects often have darker ambitions than their lofty rhetoric would suggest. Certain groups don't even bother with the lofty-sounding facade; membership in their order automatically marks one as a superior being, so why sugar-coat something that will soon be obvious once &quot;lesser beings&quot; are purged and the secret masters take their rightful place at the head of worldly affairs? It's a short step, therefore, from viewing one's self as an Awakened paragon of Enlightened Ascension, to telling one's self that anything you do in the name of that Ascension is okay in the grand scheme of things. I mean, hey - Reality will be better once the Sleeping Masses all see things your way, right...?</div> </div> </div> </div>No matter who it is or what they believe (or claim to believe), when one is endowed with power and understanding of the world, it can be so easy to convince oneself that one has all the answers. And that, further, if one has the ability to impose one's Will on the world, one has the right - nay, <i>obligation</i> - to do so. It's the same if that power is political, military, economic, or mystical.<br /> <br /> Power is a hell of a drug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:54:06-08:00","id":1291208,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy will fix the world reminds me of those times when Lex Luthor said the same to superman. if Superman would just go off and die. He'd cure cancer, he'd end poverty.. but first he has to kill superman.. for reasons. Good reasons. Really they are important. Now I'm going to spend billions of dollars making a cybersuit to fight you because of those reasons.. sure I could have made a charity instead but purple mecha suit to punch superman.<br /> <br /> What they say they want and what they actually do are two separate things. And while they totally can justify that they are making the world a better place by destroying whole cultures and committing genocide.. they are still you know committing Genocide. They are still pushing the most authoratative combination of Corporate and Political structures.<br /> <br /> I mean generally the Traditions push a level of synergy with the modern. The world of the Traditions has a place for Science and Magick. That's what they are offering. A world where you don't have to choose. Maybe this is the wrong thing for humanity. That is a possibility. I don't think its been developed as such in the setting..and many of the &quot;antiscience&quot; bits...are driven by the Technocracy as a false flag. The Syndicate explicitly pushes antivax stuff to discredit it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T14:46:09-08:00","id":1291259,"title":"","content":"\u2026and the other effect of bringing up The Technocracy is Right is that you tend to get a rather vocal response of The Traditions Are Right. That, at least, has justification in the pre-M20 editions of the game, when the Traditions were there default protagonists. But when you get right down to it, exactly the same sorts of rationales get used defending their status as the heroes as gets applied to the Union: their good points get played up, and their problematic aspects get downplayed or ignored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:37:42-08:00","id":1291289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1291187#post1291187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically, despite the 90s being known as the time of disenchantment, gamers of the time were remarkably Romantic. At least compared to the completely cynical bastards of today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Newer gamers are probably much more disenchated (cynical bastards sounds a bit exaggerated if I may say so)<br /> If I think hard about it, I'd probably choose to stand with the Traditions. Because at the end of the day I'm still a stupid Romantic that <i>believes</i> that humanity can improve and become better than it is now.<br /> <br /> Moirdryd: that's a very interesting tale, thank you for sharing. I still don't think a Technocracy game would be much appealing to me. It's a less romantic struggle, and there is less obvious ideological in-faction clash. In the Tradition you could have a party made up of a kung fu master, a mad scientist, a nun and a wizard with a pointy hat. Which I think it's cooler than being operatives that agree on methods and general philosophy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:44:39-08:00","id":1291294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1291259#post1291259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and the other effect of bringing up The Technocracy is Right is that you tend to get a rather vocal response of The Traditions Are Right. That, at least, has justification in the pre-M20 editions of the game, when the Traditions were there default protagonists. But when you get right down to it, exactly the same sorts of rationales get used defending their status as the heroes as gets applied to the Union: their good points get played up, and their problematic aspects get downplayed or ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair Revised tried to rug that under the &quot;everything wrong with the Traditions complacency went boom with Horizon&quot; thing. Even M20 paints the changes the new Traditions of the 21st century got as a step in the right direction.<br /> <br /> If anything I think that M20 did a bad favor to the Union with the whole Nephandi skeleton in the closet angle. They can be used as default now, but I thiink the flawed but ultimately human Union was more approachable than the secretly corrupted one. In some ways this was going back to a 2nd Edition narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","user":"History","date":". 02-23-2019, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T03:31:51-08:00","id":1291480,"title":"","content":"Ravnos: That was kind of the point I was making to my players who decided the technocracy were the &quot;good guys&quot; and the Traditions were obviously baddies. They soon changed their mind in view of that particular game where, yeah the Union has some interesting directives and ideals, but they are by no means benevolent or even heroic in many cases. By contrast that option exists by far more for the Traditions even if that comes at the expense of security for all humanity. <br /> <br /> TBH I love games from both sides because both can be good protagonists and antagonists, but my default always lies with the Traditions too. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T04:23:56-08:00","id":1291492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290315-how-does-consensual-reality-work-if-people-disbelieve-even-science?p=1291480#post1291480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravnos: That was kind of the point I was making to my players who decided the technocracy were the &quot;good guys&quot; and the Traditions were obviously baddies. They soon changed their mind in view of that particular game where, yeah the Union has some interesting directives and ideals, but they are by no means benevolent or even heroic in many cases. By contrast that option exists by far more for the Traditions even if that comes at the expense of security for all humanity.<br /> <br /> TBH I love games from both sides because both can be good protagonists and antagonists, but my default always lies with the Traditions too. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the advantage the Traditions have, in terms of being &quot;moral&quot;, is that they are less hierarchical. Even the Order of Hermes lets different Houses do as they please, and ditto to a certain extent for individual magi. They value their independence and autonomy heavily. And the other Trads only get MORE disorganized from there.<br /> <br /> Yes, this does mean that there's much less oversight preventing some Tradition mages from sinking to horrific lows. But it also means that Trad mages get a lot of leeway when it comes to pursuing noble goals. No one in the Tradition &quot;higher ups&quot; will begrudge, say, the Children's Crusade from crusading for children. And it's very rare for those same &quot;higher ups&quot; to mandate that individual Chantries engage in unsavory behavior, in the name of some nebulous &quot;Greater Good&quot;. Tradition campaigns have the benefit of letting players be as noble or as villainous as they please.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union is, well, a Union. Hierarchy is strict, and orders are absolute to the point where protocols are written onto members' cerebral cortexes. Their leadership is and was frequently called <b>Control </b>for a reason. They <i>controlled</i> Technocrats, and made sure everyone was on the same page. That's a non-negotiable part of being a Technocrat, and one that's going to come up constantly unless a Construct's immediate superiors were staggeringly permissive/inept (in the Union, those two are one and the same).<br /> <br /> Yes, this means that the whole Union is, more or less, kept on task, and working towards their goals. The downside is that if Control decides Technocrat PCs must go into a Trad Chantry and murder every single one of them, they will receive neither explanation for why nor any option to refuse. They can't refuse, because even their minds have been Conditioned to enforce compliance. If they rebel, they are subject to disciplinary action and even further Conditioning. Moreover, absolute power being held over loads of people will inevitably lead to abuse, as middle managers and higher ups alike exploit underlings for whatever petty, misguided, or corrupt purposes they feel like.<br /> <br /> While the evils of the Traditions are individual, the evils of the Technocracy are <i>systemic</i>. For Technocrat PCs, they are forced to be as noble or as villainous as their<i> superiors</i> please. Nor does it assume that, with an enormous apparatus of organization that the Union uses, abuses and atrocities and moral failings won't happen simply because someone, somewhere ordered it without knowing the unintended consequences, but who will not tolerate disobedience in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}